    "markdown": "---\ntitle: change\n---\n\n\n\n```python\nchange(df, variables=None, first=None, last=None)\n```\n\nThe change of each unit between two years of a panel, one row per unit.\n\n## Parameters {.doc-section .doc-section-parameters}\n\n| Name      | Type         | Description                                                                   | Default    |\n|-----------|--------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------|\n| df        | pd.DataFrame | A long panel with ``geo_id``, ``year`` and variables (e.g. from ``geo.load``) | _required_ |\n| variables |              | A variable or list of them (default: every numeric variable)                  | `None`     |\n| first     | int \\| None  | The two years to compare (default: the panel's first and last year)           | `None`     |\n| last      | int \\| None  | The two years to compare (default: the panel's first and last year)           | `None`     |\n\n## Returns {.doc-section .doc-section-returns}\n\n| Name   | Type             | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n|--------|------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n|        | pandas.DataFrame | One row per unit. For each variable ``v``: ``v_<first>``, ``v_<last>``, ``v_change`` (last minus first), ``v_pct_change`` (in percent of the first value), ``v_annual_change`` (the change divided by the years between them), ``v_rank_<first>`` and ``v_rank_<last>`` (1 = highest value) and ``v_rank_change`` (positive when the unit climbed). Text columns that are constant within a unit (``name``, ``department``...) are kept.  The years are the stored years: for panels stored at nominal years (see ``geo.reference_years``), the actual span of an indicator may differ. |\n\n## Example {.doc-section .doc-section-example}\n\n```python\n!pip install -q geo4bolivia\nimport geo4bolivia as geo\nimport plotly.express as px\n\ndf = geo.load(\"sdg01\", variables=\"sdg1_2_mpi\", groups=[\"department\"])\nchg = geo.change(df, \"sdg1_2_mpi\")\npx.scatter(chg, x=\"sdg1_2_mpi_2012\", y=\"sdg1_2_mpi_change\",\n           color=\"department\", hover_name=\"name\", labels=geo.labels(chg),\n           title=\"Poverty fell most where it was highest\")\n```\n\n::: {.g4-example-links}\n[Open a blank Colab notebook to run it](https://colab.research.google.com/notebooks/empty.ipynb)\n:::\n\n\n::: {#3134f7d6 .cell execution_count=1}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"height:525px; width:100%;\">            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/3.2.2/es5/tex-svg.min.js\"></script><script>if (window.MathJax && window.MathJax.Hub && window.MathJax.Hub.Config) {window.MathJax.Hub.Config({SVG: {font: \"STIX-Web\"}});}</script>                <script>window.PlotlyConfig = {MathJaxConfig: 'local'};</script>\n        <script charset=\"utf-8\" src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-4.1.1.m